    "created_at": "2016-11-10T19:08:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-10T19:15:12Z",
    "body": "@annevk \n\n> Sounds reasonable, this would basically make them throw slightly less? I think this does not expose a new cross-origin hole since you cannot get to the prototype object, but would be good to cinfirm.\n\nWhere can I find a reference about the security issue that this is addressing?\n\n> Also, should WindowProxy still define this if Window takes care of it anyway?\n\nSeems like we could either forward it to the Window, or just stop it here. I don't think there's an observable difference, and they'd be around the same amount of text.\n\n> Also, the way IDL does this is slightly ugly I think. Should we not just add an abstract operation to ECMAScript and make all [[SetPrototypeOf]] definitions that share it refer to that?\n\nThat refactoring sounds like a good idea. I'll try to get that in before this patch.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
